# Mutation plan for the six wsapi actions and the socket lifecycle around them (2026-09-15).
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/websocket-actions.plan
#
# Worth mutating: Go's lenient type rules (a non-string is empty, not refused), the two unchecked
# assertions in posted_notify_ack, the decoder that reads one value, the auth window, the user id a
# challenge must set, the status cache write-back, and the defaults a reader could flip. The last two
# lines are no-op controls and must SURVIVE.
#
# Not planned, with reasons: is_valid_id on channel_id is equivalent under test (an invalid id fails
# the permission lookup with the same refusal); the pong-away spawn and the no-reset-on-text read
# deadline need a 60s and a 100s wait; the wrapper session re-read is shadowed by hub invalidation
# on every same-server revocation the suite can produce.
